# Cloudflare Pages routing rule.
#
# Restructured 2026-08-27 (see docs/idealization_report.md, 2026-08-26 and
# 2026-08-27 sprints). The Vite build now emits dist/index.html (the public
# marketing landing page, physically at the build root) and dist/app.html
# (the operational 3D canvas app — requires a LAN-local backend, never
# meant to be what a public domain root serves).
#
# Root ("/") needs no rule here: it's served directly from the literal
# index.html Cloudflare Pages always treats as the implicit root document
# — no redirect involved. This one rule gives the operational app a clean
# extension-less URL (/app) matching how Cloudflare's own HTML-file
# canonicalization already wants to present it, rather than fighting that
# behavior the way the old `/ -> /landing.html` rewrite did (that rewrite's
# 200 response was itself re-canonicalized into a visible 308 to /landing
# — root-caused in the 2026-08-26 sprint entry; this restructure is that
# fix). Confirmed live post-deploy: see the 2026-08-27 sprint entry for the
# actual curl-verified redirect/status-code results.
/app /app.html 200
